  "id": "09-kernel-in-archon",
  "title": "Kernel concepts mapped onto Archon",
  "description": "Maps the agent kernel's ten concepts (left, teal section, grouped into Definition and execution / Run records / Read and route surfaces) onto Archon's seven concepts (middle, pink section), per the page \"Where the Kernel Fits in Archon\". Each wire runs from a kernel concept to its nearest Archon counterpart and is colored and labeled with its verdict: green = same idea, orange = partial, blue = kernel has it/Archon does not, violet = Archon has it/kernel does not. Token Gateway (gray) has no link; its note sits level with it, right of the kernel section. The kernel source note runs along the bottom from the kernel section's edge. The right column holds the key, the Gaps neither side has section (gray nodes) and the Archon source note. The kernel–Archon band is kept at its 820 px rule number for its 11 labelled wires.",
